y  else's an opportunity which would soon  present itself the second reason was  liberia across the previous century  american patrons had helped to fund  friedman's journeys to africa to found a  territory for freed slaves in 1822 this  culminated in the creation of liberia  which was sort of an american colony but  also totally wasn't as such it just sort  of sat in limbo it eventually got sick  of america ignoring it and it declared  its independence in 1847. however it  maintained very good relations with the  united states and after this alongside  the congo the us had much of the access  to africa for missionaries and trade  that it had wanted the third reason was  that american desire to spread its  influence beyond its own borders was  mostly limited to its neighbors in south  america all of this being under the  monroe doctrine this was a pledge by the  united states to protect the americas in  any independent state there from  european expansion or coercion providing  that you exclude the british claiming  the falklands mexico being run by an  austrian briefly and venezuela seeding  land to britain and so with that the  united states just sort of sat the  scramble for africa out much like their  european cousins the americans were also  interested in the resources and  conversion of africa but unlike  europeans americans felt like they  already had hegemony over two continents  and thus they had no desire to squabble  over pieces of a third i hope you  enjoyed this episode and a special  thanks to my patrons james bisonette  kelly money maker skye chappelle corso  wolff jordan longley adam stalter jerry  lambda marcus arsenault words about  books podcast rodney martin lion hockey  marvin castell spencer lightfoot  boogerly wiggly winston k wood captain  cydol kim moon yoon gustav swan daniel  to be in misses at aaron the white  matthew shipley maggie patzkowski alex  schwinn corey turner anthony beckett  coppertone schwennin spinning three  plates the mcqu